stdarg.h comes from GCC 2.95.2, gcc/ginclude/stdarg.h.
va-ppc.h derives from EGCS 1.1.2, gcc/ginclude/va-ppc.h, with the va_start block
from GCC 2.95.2's same file. These are GNU compiler project sources. Their
original comments are retained; the upstream GNU General Public License v2
text is supplied as COPYING. See config/GR8E69/newlib-source.json for source
URLs and hashes, and docs/Newlib.md for the observed ABI and modifications.

stddef.h, limits.h and float.h are minimal target declarations authored for this
reconstruction. Only their use by the accepted source units has been verified.
This is not a complete historical compiler header distribution.
